From 1ef0edc4c45353c4946c0e1acc525a4314bc507b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abhishek <a.dandekar@tu.berlin>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:30:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(smf): PCF-initiated PDU session modification for dynamic
 QoS flows

Honour SmPolicyUpdateNotification (TS 29.512 4.2.4.2) from the PCF, e.g.
triggered by an N5 Npcf_PolicyAuthorization app session (MCPTT AF), and run
the PCF-initiated PDU Session Modification of TS 23.502 4.3.3.2:

- New PCC rules (with their QoS decision) create a dedicated QoS flow: new
  QFI, one N3/N6 edge pair per flow information on the session UPF (same N3
  tunnel), N4 Session Modification with Create PDR/FAR/QER (UL and/or DL per
  flowDirection, shared UL/DL QER with MBR/GBR and QFI).
- Changed QoS decisions (e.g. ARP) update the QERs (Update QER) and the QoS
  flow; changed packet filters re-create the flow.
- PCC rules set to null (TS 29.512) release the flow: Remove PDR/FAR/QER and
  the edges/IDs/QFI.
- After the N4 response, Namf_Communication_N1N2MessageTransfer with N2 PDU
  Session Resource Modify Request Transfer (QoS Flow Add or Modify Request
  List / QoS Flow to Release List) and N1 PDU Session Modification Command
  (QoS rules + QoS flow descriptions create/modify/delete, PTI 0).
- The PCF gets 200 OK after the N4 modification (500 + roll-back if the UPF
  rejects it).

Fixes found on the way:
- the HTTP/2 callback route /nsmf-callback/v1 only matched the exact path,
  so the notificationUri advertised to the PCF always returned 404
- callback body accumulated over several DATA frames, null map entries of
  the SmPolicyDecision tolerated, error responses had no status
- N1: Authorized QoS rules / QoS flow descriptions were encoded without IEI
- reuse the SMF-allocated N3 F-TEID when the UPF has no F-TEID allocation
- PDU Session Resource Modify Response without new DL tunnel no longer
  re-creates FAR/PDRs (and zeroes the gNB F-TEID)

Limitations: only PDU sessions served by a single UPF (N3<->N6); UE side
(NAS PDU Session Modification Complete) not exercised.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
